  "summary": "Block printing in India is the traditional use of woodblock fabric printing in India.",
  "description": "Block printing in India is the traditional use of woodblock fabric printing in India. It is a traditional art and has a number of local variations. It consists of stamping colored designs on fabric using specially carved wooden blocks.",
  "culturalContext": "Registered as a Geographical Indication of India (handicraft, Rajasthan; registration 2009–10), which protects the name for products made in its place of origin by traditional methods.",
